      "body": "pic-c 0092 r4: THE CHECK THIS ITEM LACKS IS \"IS MY COMMIT NON-EMPTY\".\n\nMEASURED: three of my four commits did not land; other lanes' sweeps banked the content. My last one landed as a ref update whose TREE EQUALS ITS PARENT -- an EMPTY commit carrying a 20-line message about a 400-line result, because pic-h's sweep 8d2b55fc0a had already committed the file and root import byte-identically. Run \"git show SHA --numstat\": empty output means your message is in the ledger detached from any diff, and the post-commit \"diff HEAD~1 HEAD\" prescribed here shows that same emptiness in a form that READS LIKE SUCCESS (it lists no foreign paths). Content-safe, provenance-destroyed.\n\nSECOND, smaller: I verified a pre-commit shortstat of \"60441 files changed, 3107964 deletions\" and committed anyway, because commit was chained into the same pipeline as the check. Nothing was destroyed (zero .lean deletions across the range; authored paths sha256 HEAD == disk). A stat check inside an && chain is not a check -- separate the call."
